{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLZnyoxZiFwwnSx6edUV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made the finding-decode errors content-free, and `go test ./internal/scanner/` passes. I didn't run `make test`. Decode errors now carry only a line number and a fixed reason class, such as `fingerprint: invalid UTF-8 or control characters` or `file: not repo-relative (absolute, unclean or contains ..)`.\n\n- **JSON library errors:** `decodeStrict` in `internal/scanner/decode.go` no longer wraps the `encoding/json` error text, because that text can quote scanner input. It now maps the error to `invalid JSON`, `wrong value type`, `unknown key` or `malformed`.\n- **Quoted values removed:** the fingerprint, severity, file and duplicate-fingerprint errors in `internal/scanner/finding.go` no longer quote the value. The duplicate message now gives only the line of the first occurrence.\n- **Tests:** I updated the expected substrings in `internal/scanner/finding_test.go` and added `TestDecodeErrorsNeverEchoScannerText`. It uses a secret-shaped marker across fingerprint, file, unknown-key, severity, wrong-type, non-JSON, truncated and trailing-data cases. It also includes a case with several bad lines. Each case checks that the marker is absent, the reason text is present and the line number is right.\n\nI dropped the planned bad-UTF-8 case. `encoding/json` replaces invalid bytes with U+FFFD before validation, so no error is produced and there is nothing to test.\n\nThis overlaps with #215 around scan-failed logging, so rebase if it lands first.\n\nI wrote the report to `.ard/231/worker-engineer.md`. It reads \"Only the scanner package was tested\", which holds up. It doesn't mention that `git status` also shows the untracked `.ard-input/231/` files. I didn't create those; the controller put them there."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"c